            <ArticleTitle>Synthesis of 3-(Arylsulfonyl)benzothiophenes and Benzoselenophenes via TBHP-Initiated Radical Cyclization of 2-Alkynylthioanisoles or -selenoanisoles with Sulfinic Acids.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>6292-6295</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1021/acs.orglett.7b02971</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>tert-Butyl hydroperoxide-initiated radical cyclization of 2-alkynylthioanisoles or -selenoanisoles with sulfinic acids has been developed. This reaction is applicable to a wide substrate scope via one C(sp3)-S(Se) bond cleavage and two C(sp2)-S(Se) bond formation, leading to the synthesis of 3-(arylsulfonyl)benzothiophenes or -benzoselenophenes under mild conditions.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
